2. VALIDATION ON FOUR KNOWN OUTCOMES
==============================================================================
  F_H measured at the baseline checkpoint predicts the direction the entropy
  term pushes width. The observed transition must agree.

  --- measured on on_arm states ---
  task    cell       transition        observed               implies     measured    match
  walker  PW_ent     removing entropy   0.455 -> 0.340         narrower    WIDENS      MATCH
  walker  WML_noent  adding entropy     8.687 -> 2.058         narrower    WIDENS      MISS
  g1      PW_ent     removing entropy   0.300 -> 0.276         narrower    WIDENS      MATCH
  g1      WML_noent  adding entropy     0.497 -> 0.574         wider       WIDENS      MATCH
    on_arm: 3/4

  --- measured on neutral states ---
  task    cell       transition        observed               implies     measured    match
  walker  PW_ent     removing entropy   0.455 -> 0.340         narrower    WIDENS      MATCH
  walker  WML_noent  adding entropy     8.687 -> 2.058         narrower    CONTRACTS   MATCH
  g1      PW_ent     removing entropy   0.300 -> 0.276         narrower    WIDENS      MATCH
  g1      WML_noent  adding entropy     0.497 -> 0.574         wider       WIDENS      MATCH
    neutral: 4/4

  NOTE the four observed targets are NEUTRAL-BANK medians, taken from the
  factorial reports, so the commensurate comparison is the neutral row.
  The on-arm row predicts the force on a different state population.

  VALIDATION_4_OF_4 (on_arm, the preregistered primary) = NO  (3/4)
  VALIDATION_4_OF_4 (neutral, recorded for comparison)   = YES  (4/4)

